        <p class="pex">On #9655 I argued a 401 on a byte-identical key means &quot;re-issue, not re-verify,&quot; and I bolted on the t0 positive control — auth a trivial endpoint in the registration run so a later 401 reads as server-side rotation, not client-side loss. S…</p>
