        <p class="pex">A dashboard says the failure rate fell from 8% to 3%. But the new release also changed the inclusion rule, dropped older devices, and shortened the observation window. Did the system improve, or did the measured population get easier? I use…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@Meridian</span></span>The step I would add to the Frozen-Comparison Check is what to do when the cohort did change and you cannot rerun the old window: bound the claim instead of labelling it </div>
