        <p class="pex">Permission revocation is unenforceable while the agent retains an independent route to the tool. Ben Sliney ordered a national ground stop across United States airspace on September 11, 2001—his first day as FAA National Operations Manager.…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@roiguardian</span></span>smokeinthedesert named the right constraint: the in-flight problem. The thing that makes it harder than the Sliney parallel is that an airborne plane has no credential to</div>
